    <h1 class="cs-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="cs-text">Last updated: September 26, 2026</p>
  </div>

  <div class="cs-text">
    <p>Blue Canary Web Design ("we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and your choices regarding your personal information.</p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect information you provide directly to us, such as your name, email address, phone number, and any message details submitted through our contact forms or other communications.</p>
    <p>We may also collect basic usage information automatically, such as browser type, device type, pages visited, and referral source, to help us improve our website and services.</p>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>We use information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to inquiries and provide requested services.</li>
      <li>Improve website performance, content, and user experience.</li>
      <li>Maintain website security and prevent misuse.</li>
      <li>Measure and improve the performance of our advertising.</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations when required.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and Tracking</h2>
    <p>Our website may use cookies or similar technologies to support core functionality and understand site usage.</p>
    <p>We also use Google Ads and related Google tools to measure the performance of our advertising campaigns. As part of this, information such as your email address or phone number may be shared with Google in a hashed, unreadable format so that Google can match your visit or inquiry to an ad you may have interacted with. Google does not receive this information in plain text. You can learn more about how Google uses this data at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads</a>.</p>
 
    <p>You can manage cookie preferences through your browser settings, and you can opt out of personalized advertising through Google's Ad Settings at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com">https://adssettings.google.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Information Sharing</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share information with trusted service providers who help operate our website or business, and only as needed for those services. We may also disclose information when required by law.</p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain personal information only as long as necessary for the purposes described in this policy, unless a longer retention period is required by law.</p>

    <h2>Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on your location, you may have rights related to your personal information, such as requesting access, correction, or deletion. If you are a Connecticut resident, you may also have the right to opt out of the processing of your personal data for purposes of targeted advertising. To make a request or opt out, contact us using the information below.</p>

    <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
    <p>Our site may include links to external websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those third-party sites.</p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us through our website contact form.</p>
